{"id":"twitter:1727350815311155271","tweet_id":"1727350815311155271","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1727350815311155271","title":"@dromanocpm I just had chance to read this. I would avoid the word \"form\" even if semantically correct. Feels like a SOC 2 questionnaire. It needs to ","summary":"@dromanocpm I just had chance to read this. I would avoid the word \"form\" even if semantically correct. Feels like a SOC 2 questionnaire. It needs to be language of continuous authorization (yes I know modells.txt would be dynamic) There is already work towards this with SBOMs and OSCAL","date":"2023-11-22","published":"2023-11-22T15:38:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/dromanocpm/status/1727162442679976008","reply_tweet_id":"1727162442679976008","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@dromanocpm I just had chance to read this.<br><br>I would avoid the word &quot;form&quot; even if semantically correct. <br><br>Feels like a SOC 2 questionnaire. It needs to be language of continuous authorization (yes I know modells.txt would be dynamic)<br><br>There is already work towards this with SBOMs and OSCAL</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1727350815311155271","display_date":"November 22, 2023 · 15:38 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
